In **Android Gradle Plugin (AGP) 9.0**, the legacy `applicationVariants` API and direct `outputFileName` manipulation have been removed[1][2][3]. To rename APKs, you must move away from modifying the build output directly and instead use the **`androidComponents`** API[4][5].

### Recommended Approach
Because AGP 9.0 does not support direct manipulation of output file names, the recommended approach is to **copy the generated APK to a new file name** using a custom task finalized by the build process[6][7][3].

#### Implementation Strategy
You should use the `androidComponents.onVariants` block to register a task that triggers after the APK is assembled[7][3].

```kotlin
// In your app/build.gradle.kts
androidComponents {
    onVariants { variant ->
        val capitalizedName = variant.name.replaceFirstChar { it.uppercase() }
        val renameTask = tasks.register("renameApk${capitalizedName}") {
            // Define your custom naming logic here
            val newFileName = "MyApp_${variant.name}_${project.version}.apk"

            doLast {
                val apkDir = layout.buildDirectory.dir("outputs/apk/${variant.name}").get().asFile
                apkDir.listFiles()?.filter { it.extension == "apk" }?.forEach { apk ->
                    apk.copyTo(File(apk.parentFile, newFileName), overwrite = true)
                    println("Renamed: ${apk.name} -> $newFileName")
                }
            }
        }

        // Ensure the rename task runs after the assemble task
        afterEvaluate {
            tasks.named("assemble${capitalizedName}") {
                finalizedBy(renameTask)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

